cctools 806 for OPENSTEP/i386

This package supplies ar, ranlib, and the classic cctools linker. It builds
with stock /bin/cc and has no GCC 4.2 dependency, so gcc42 can depend on it.
The cctools-as package supplies the assembler separately.

Install with: sh ./pkg install cctools
Test with:    sh ./pkg test cctools

The matched tools live in /usr/local/lib/cctools/bin. The public commands
are ar-806, ranlib-806, and ld-806. Package builds select AR and RANLIB
explicitly. ar runs the matching ranlib from that private directory.

The gcc42 package configures this linker directly when rebuilt. An existing
Apple GCC 4.2 installation can select it explicitly with
-specs=/usr/local/lib/cctools/gcc42.specs. This changes only the linker and
can be combined with cctools-as's assembler specs. Do not install this
partial specs file as GCC's default specs file; GCC expects a complete
specification there.

Rebuild an existing gcc42 installation to make this linker its default.
Since pkg skips an installed package with the same version,
run "sh ./pkg build NAME" first; after it succeeds, run "sh ./pkg remove NAME",
"sh ./pkg install NAME", and "sh ./pkg test NAME".

Stock /bin/cc, ar, ranlib, and ld remain available. The stock compiler
hardcodes its linker, so it cannot link archives with extended member names.
Its bootstrap libraries use /bin/ar and /bin/ranlib. Libraries with
extended member names require the matching cctools archive tools and linker.
Do not run stock ranlib on a long-name archive: it cannot index its members.

The native linker uses 8 KB segments and a flat namespace, and omits UUID
load commands. These match OPENSTEP's executable format. Optional LLVM
bitcode support is outside this native Mach-O toolchain build.

The patch adds private BSD/libc compatibility routines, uses Mach map_fd
for private file mappings, and retains 32-bit OPENSTEP archive offsets.
The package is intended for native i386 OPENSTEP output.

The ar sources include software developed by the University of California,
Berkeley and its contributors. Copyright and license notices remain in the
upstream source; the Apple license and tool manuals are installed here.

Validated on 2026-10-19, OPENSTEP 4.2/i386 at 192.168.1.76, as user me:
  - cctools built with stock cc, installed, and passed its package test:
    distinct long names, replacement/deletion, extraction/repacking,
    old-format archives, odd-sized members, malformed-input rejection,
    native execution, and relocatable linking.
  - gcc42 completed its three-stage bootstrap. Both upstream comparisons
    passed; the strict comparison checked 612 pairs, with 608 exact matches,
    four upstream exclusions, and no failures.
  - The installed GCC C, C++, Objective-C, and Objective-C++ regressions
    passed using the new linker and newly built runtime archives.
  - cctools-as rebuilt and passed its instruction-byte, relocation,
    mixed-object, C++, and Objective-C tests with the new linker.
  - The patch applies cleanly to pristine cctools-806.
